2026-08-16T11:32:46Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: Wrong basis: the +12.05% YoY uplift is taken from FY2022Q3→FY2023Q3, but Deere’s most recent same‑quarter comp shows FY2025Q3 “Worldwide net sales and revenues” DOWN 9% YoY to $12,018m. Applying a positive double‑digit YoY to project FY2026Q3 off that base ignores the current downcycle evident in the latest reported quarter for the same period, making $13,465.9m likely overstated. This is checkable against Deere’s FY2025 Q3 press release citing the −9% to $12.018 billion.
2026-08-16T11:32:52Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: The blend is anchored to an unsupported “guidance_anchor+signal” of 3,929.25 USDm, while the only cited guidance says “we are forecasting revenue of $3.9 billion, +/- $100 million,” i.e., a 3,900 USDm midpoint. Using 3,929.25 as the anchor (weighted 96.9%) inflates the estimate by ~28.34 USDm; applying your same weights to the documented 3,900 USDm midpoint and 2,813.07 seasonal input yields ~3,866.31 USDm, not 3,894.64. The proposed number is thus based on the wrong guidance figure.
2026-08-16T11:33:03Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: no concrete objection found
2026-08-16T11:33:08Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: Your “median YoY growth” is miscomputed. With the two stated observations −14.0% (FY2023→FY2024) and −12.7% (FY2024→FY2025), the median (average of the two central values when n=2) is −13.35%, not −13.33%. Applying −13.35% to the reported FY2025 base £972.4m gives £842.4m, not £842.8m, so the proposed £842.775m is overstated by roughly £0.4m.
2026-08-16T11:33:20Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: The -1.4% “post‑guidance tilt” violates your own ±6.0% cap given the listed signals (-0.70, -0.50, +0.50). Any reasonable aggregation (mean = -0.233, median = -0.50) would hit the negative cap, so the tilt should be -6.0%, not -1.4%. Applying the cap to the 3.58704 base gives 3.58704 × (1 − 0.06) = 3.37182, not 3.53682—your EPS is therefore too high.
2026-08-16T11:33:30Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: You mixed periods in the growth input: the -64.9% figure is an H1 2026 year-on-year change, not a full-year FY-to-FY change, yet it was included to compute the median YoY and then applied to the full-year FY2025 EPS of 1.31p to estimate full-year FY2026. Using an H1 change alongside full-year changes (FY2023→FY2024 and FY2024→FY2025) is a wrong basis for a full-year forecast and likely biases the result.
2026-08-16T11:33:31Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Wrong basis: the anchor “$4.68 for FY2025 Q2” is the company’s reported GAAP diluted EPS, not an “adjusted” EPS. Home Depot typically reports GAAP diluted EPS and did not publish a separate adjusted diluted EPS for FY2025 Q2. Using a GAAP figure to forecast an adjusted metric makes the FY2026 Q2 ‘adjusted diluted EPS’ of 4.68001 on the wrong basis. Verify against Home Depot’s FY2025 Q2 earnings release/8‑K, which cites diluted EPS of $4.68 and no non‑GAAP adjusted EPS reconciliation for that quarter.
2026-08-16T11:33:31Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: You weighted a “guidance_anchor+signal” of 3.3594 for FY2026Q3, but the only documented guidance you cite is a midpoint of $3.30 (range $3.15–$3.45). Using the cited $3.30 midpoint in your weights (3.30×0.969 + 2.0256×0.031) gives about $3.2605 per share, not $3.3180. The proposed value is therefore based on an unsupported guidance input and is biased high relative to the stated source.
2026-08-16T11:33:37Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: You used “FY2025Q3 (13.6)” as the prior-year operating profit in USDm, but the source shows 13.6% is an operating margin, not a dollar profit. Applying a -98.83% YoY change (itself seemingly derived from the margin shift 22.8%→13.6%, not from profit dollars) to a percentage produced 0.159m, which is a unit/basis error. For FY2025Q3, the required base should be operating profit in USDm, not the 13.6% margin.
